      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Thanks!\nI took a moment to look into why my AFK state was tripping up here and found these preexisting bugs:\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/avatar-30/p/bug-opening-steam-menu-in-vrfbt-causes-weird-afk-state\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/bug-reports/p/opening-steamvr-menu-enables-afk-parameter-twice\nIt turns out that my animator was getting stuck in a tracking state due to a slow transition when exiting and re-entering AFK. I had been relying on SteamVR overlay disabling my tracking to compensate for this, but I was able to add an extra transition to my animator for an even smoother solution.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-05-13T03:07:21.380Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Recent betas have included a fix where \"Users will no longer lose tracking when opening the SteamVR overlay.\"\nI think it would be helpful to have the option of disabling this feature so that opening the SteamVR overlay can disable tracking again if desired.",
